# (after 0517) host/offline: four offline service answers (streamplay HID feature query, prepo idle transmission, friend-ID / network Result hooks, friends no-Uid and blocked-user forms)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/b768913fd08fb7b62cc69b00b23b42ff813dc17b  ("host/streamplay: serve the supported HID feature query (PR #3162)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 23:34 +0800; Co-authored-by: Benjyp
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/1364b89a498fb78af42c8d42e7beebbd3bbd5de6  ("host/prepo: report idle transmission offline (PR #2908)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 01:15 +0800; Co-authored-by: heavn-r
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/656f8844021012649c5ed3d603180f3676f295ef  ("host/offline: register friend-ID and network Result hooks (PR #3119)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 02:12 +0800; Co-authored-by: PikaMan80, Eliran Zach
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/977f5cab3a1357a3995fd57c72e43acaa4618034  ("host/friends: hook blocked-user availability, no-Uid forms, and cut-object methods")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 00:21 +0800; Co-authored-by: Anderson Souza
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: each call reached a Nintendo service the host does not run and the SDK aborted with 0xe15 (or entered the service): Star Fox's nn::streamplay::GetSupportedHidFeatureSet
#   (PR #3162), Nintendo Switch Sports' play-report transmission status after a Chambara win (PR #2908), Super Kirby Clash 1.0.1's account-ID friend lists and
#   ShowNetworkServiceError(nn::Result) (PR #3119), SUPER BOMBERMAN R 2 1.0.0's EnsureBlockedUserListAvailable at the title screen (issue #3177).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/host/hle_misc.c, hle_offline.c, hle_friends.c; tests t_pctl, t_server_environment, t_friends):
#   streamplay: SetSupportedHidFeatureSet keeps its 32-bit mask, a GetSupportedHidFeatureSet takeover returns it. prepo: transmission status idle. offline: the two friend-ID list exports fail
#   with zero entries and leave the ID array, ShowNetworkServiceError logs the Result and sends the usual applet notifications. friends: 13 more nn::friends symbols under the offline policy
#   (blocked-user availability with and without Uid, no-Uid overloads, Friend::Update, AsyncContext::Cancel).
# Adapted: 977f5cab's NotificationQueue::Initialize() / Clear() / Finalize() hooks are NOT taken (they fail the queue); engine-patches/0513 already hooks them with its own meaning
#   (the queue opens and stays empty, Beach Buggy Racing 2), and 0513 stays as it is. The upstream t_friends block is ported without its NotificationQueue lines (0513 checks those).
#   One patch for the four commits (the review's candidates 0518, 0519, 0520 and 0523, which apply in a row on disjoint hunks).
# Games: Star Fox (0400E88025B1A000), Nintendo Switch Sports, Super Kirby Clash, SUPER BOMBERMAN R 2; any game that asks the same. Switches: none.
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_friends 61 checks (0513's and 977f5cab's), t_pctl, t_server_environment, all in the host-unit run of HOST_TESTS. NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0517, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

